WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.180
ANU SRIVASTAVA:
Today, we're talking

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:05.810
about Google I/O announcements,
Applied ML Summit, and Cloud

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:06.920
SQL maintenance.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.590
I'm Anu, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:13.140
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.480
We're still basking
in the afterglow

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.670
of Google I/O. And did
you know that there were

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.650
tons of Cloud announcements?

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.700
Head to the blog for a list
of keynotes, topics, and links

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.200
to on-demand sessions.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.890
There's everything from machine
learning, to cloud run jobs,

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.410
and even how to increase
your productivity

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.680
with Google Workspace.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.770
At Google Cloud, we've
helped thousands of companies

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:40.520
accelerate their AI efforts,
empower their data scientists,

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.550
and extend the ability
to build AI-driven apps

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.390
and workflows to more people.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.830
This includes everyone, no data
science or machine learning

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.370
background required.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:54.740
So please join us June 9 for the
Google Cloud Applied ML Summit,

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.020
a digital event which
will bring together

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.890
some of the world's leading ML
and data science professionals,

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:04.040
all to explore the
latest cutting edge AI

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.030
tools for developing,
deploying, and managing machine

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.740
learning models at scale.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.530
Register today.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:16.070
Cloud SQL has now made
self-service maintenance

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.580
generally available.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.630
This allows you the freedom
to upgrade your Cloud SQL

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:23.930
instance's maintenance
version to the latest version.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.810
The benefit is that you can
receive the latest security

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.560
patches, bug fixes, and
new features on demand.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.020
When combined with deny
maintenance periods,

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:36.380
self-service maintenance
gives you the flexibility

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.240
to upgrade your
instance according

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.870
to your own
maintenance schedule.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.240
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.560
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.060
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.800
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.300
We'll see you in the Cloud.

